   "id": "n-ga-077",
   "subject": "gross-anatomy",
   "title": "Lab · Back Muscles Moina · Superficial & Intermediate Layers",
   "body": "*Moina = Muscle · Origin · Insertion · Nerve · Action*\n\n## Nerve quick-recall\n- Trapezius → spinal accessory nerve (CN XI)\n- Latissimus dorsi → thoracodorsal nerve (C6–C8)\n- Levator scapulae, rhomboids → dorsal scapular nerve\n- Serratus posterior → intercostal nerves (ventral rami)\n- All deep back muscles → posterior rami of spinal nerves\n- Suboccipitals → suboccipital nerve (dorsal ramus of C1)\n- Pectorals → pectoral nerves (brachial plexus)\n- Rectus abdominis → lower 6 thoracic nerves\n- Obliques, transversus → lower 6 thoracic + iliohypogastric / ilioinguinal (L1)\n- Psoas, quadratus lumborum → lumbar plexus\n\n## Superficial layer (extrinsic, connect upper limb to trunk)\n### Trapezius (superficial; moves scapula)\n- **O:** medial third of superior nuchal line, external occipital protuberance, ligamentum nuchae, spinous processes of C7–T12\n- **I:** lateral third of clavicle, acromion, spine of scapula\n- **N:** spinal accessory nerve (CN XI); C3–C4 (pain and proprioception)\n- **A:** elevates, retracts and rotates scapula (upward rotation). Descending part elevates, middle part retracts, ascending part depresses\n### Latissimus dorsi (climbing muscle)\n- **O:** spinous processes of T7–T12, thoracolumbar fascia, iliac crest, inferior 3–4 ribs\n- **I:** floor of intertubercular sulcus of humerus\n- **N:** thoracodorsal nerve (C6–C8)\n- **A:** extends, adducts and medially rotates humerus; raises body toward arms during climbing\n### Levator scapulae\n- **O:** posterior tubercles of transverse processes of C1–C4\n- **I:** medial border of scapula superior to the root of the spine (superior angle)\n- **N:** dorsal scapular nerve (C5); cervical nerves (C3–C4)\n- **A:** elevates scapula; tilts glenoid cavity inferiorly (downward rotation)\n### Rhomboid minor\n- **O:** ligamentum nuchae, spinous processes of C7–T1\n- **I:** medial border of scapula at the root of the spine\n- **N:** dorsal scapular nerve (C4–C5)\n- **A:** retracts scapula, rotates glenoid cavity downward, fixes scapula to thoracic wall\n### Rhomboid major\n- **O:** spinous processes of T2–T5\n- **I:** medial border of scapula from the spine to the inferior angle\n- **N:** dorsal scapular nerve (C4–C5)\n- **A:** retracts scapula, rotates glenoid cavity downward, fixes scapula to thoracic wall\n\n## Intermediate layer (extrinsic, respiratory)\n### Serratus posterior superior (inspiratory)\n- **O:** ligamentum nuchae, spinous processes of C7–T3\n- **I:** superior borders of ribs 2–4\n- **N:** 2nd–5th intercostal nerves (ventral rami of upper thoracic nerves)\n- **A:** elevates ribs\n### Serratus posterior inferior (expiratory)\n- **O:** spinous processes of T11–L2\n- **I:** inferior borders of ribs 9–12\n- **N:** ventral rami of T9–T12 (lower intercostal and subcostal nerves)\n- **A:** depresses ribs",
   "order": 77,
   "updated": 1794880000000
